<h2>Introduction To Java</h2>
<p>Java is a high-level programming language developed by Sun
Microsystems in 1995.
It is known for its platform independence, meaning programs written in
Java can run
on different operating systems such as Windows, Linux and Mac.

</p>
<h3>Key Features Of Java</h3>
<ul>
 <li>Object-Oreinted Programing</li>
 <li>Secure and Reliable</li>
 <li>Simple and Easy to learn</li>
 <li>Platform Independent</li>
</ul>
<h5>Why i select java language?</h5>
<p>Because it is a powerful and reliable programming language. It helps
in creating dynamic and interactive web applications. Java is secure
and widely used, which makes it a good choice for building strong
backend systems. It also works on different platforms, so the website
can run easily on various devices. Overall, Java makes the website more
efficient and easy to manage.
</p>
<br>
<h3>Advantages Of Java</h3>
<ol>
<li>Write Once Run Anywhere</li>
<li>Large developer community</li>
<li>Used for Android development</li>
<li>High security features</li>
</ol>
<hr>
<h2>Future Scope Of Java</h2>
<p>The future scope of Java is very strong and promising. Here are some
key points:</p>
<p>
<br><b>Web and Mobile Development</b> – Java is widely used for
building websites, web applications, and Android mobile apps.</p>
<p><br><b>Enterprise Applications</b> – Many big companies use Java
for large-scale business software because it is reliable and
secure.</p>
<p><br><b>Cloud Computing</b> – Java is used in cloud-based
applications and services due to its platform independence.<p>
<p><br><b>Big Data and AI</b> – Java works well with big data tools
(like Hadoop) and is also used in machine learning and AI projects.
</p>
<p><br><b>High Demand Jobs </b> – Java developers are always in demand,
so learning Java gives good career opportunities worldwide</p>
